Z||000002||longjonsilver||11-22-2001||12:15 PM||||great!  but there is no numver with WA_ _ _ _ on the left front fender.  there is a white lable with a jillion other numbers and a aluminum plaque in front of the fender but no WA number.  any other ideas?  white 84 2m4<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by WampusCat:<BR><B> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/014296.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/014296.html</A> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierobruiser||11-22-2001||01:52 PM||||WA-40 find them all at this site in the Technical Database under Paint codes. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.mn.org/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.mn.org/</A> <P>------------------<BR>Notchbacks Rule<BR>85GT(show car)<BR>88Coupe (daily driver)<BR>84 Coupe(project car)||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||11-22-2001||07:14 PM||||its the last number, its either at the end of list or at the very bottom edge. All GM cars/trucks have it since late 70s. Always 4 digits preceded by WA. Thats what body shops use for finding colors. Alternate is if you have the stamped metal plate, it will normally be a 2 digit number with a 'U' or 'L' (for upper and lower color)<BR>*special note too, if for example plate has 40U, be aware that there may be several different shades of that color avail from GM, so may not match. WA# is specific for that car.<P>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 11-22-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 11-23-2001).]||||reg||1
